WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
(soldiers shouting)
(guns firing)

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.710
- [Narrator] This video
posted to social media

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.780
by a Ukrainian Battalion

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.250
claims to show their soldiers

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.440
crossing the Dnipro River by boat

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.090
into Russian occupied territory

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.790
in Southern Ukraine in January.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.974
(soldiers shouting)
(guns firing)

00:00:19.974 --> 00:00:22.710
An example of the risky
cross river operations

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.923
that Ukraine has stepped
up in recent weeks.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.400
The Dnipro River runs through Ukraine

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.860
from its northern border through Kherson

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.600
and into the Black Sea.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.790
It has served as the southern front line

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.890
dividing Ukrainian and Russian forces

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.930
for the last several months.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.600
For Ukraine, penetrating
this part of the front line

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.553
is critical for two reasons.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.860
First, it prevents Russia

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.390
from sending troops stationed there

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.340
to other areas of the front.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.160
And second, regaining
lands south of the river

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.050
would disrupt Russians supply lines

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.873
and bring Ukrainian troops
to Crimea's doorstep.

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:02.200
(artillery shuffling)

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.930
(boots thudding)
(engine purring)

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.910
Ukrainian raid teams have been challenging

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.830
Russians control here for months

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.450
according to analysts from Janes

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.624
and the Institute for
the Study of War, or ISW.

00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:15.311
(soldiers shouting)

00:01:15.311 --> 00:01:18.060
An analyst from Janes says
that during a typical raid

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.890
small boats likely cross the river

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.530
a few kilometers from
their desired landing,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.300
and then ride along the bank.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.160
The unit would then
disembark from the boat

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.560
at least a kilometer from any target

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.813
and infiltrate the rest
of the way on foot.

00:01:33.362 --> 00:01:35.040
(gun firing)

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.010
These attacks have
increased in recent weeks.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:41.010
By the beginning of August,
Ukrainians launched a new effort

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.073
near the Russian occupied
village of Kozachi Laheri.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.060
Video posted on August 9th to Telegram

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.340
by a Ukrainian reconnaissance team

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.670
shows an artillery barrage on
the outskirts of the village,

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.283
possibly the precursor
to one of these raids.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.010
Another clip posted that same day

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.990
appears to show a Russian combat vehicle

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.523
under fire nearby.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.340
ISW's mapping of the front lines

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.580
shows Ukrainians claiming
ground west of Kozachi Laheri

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.263
on August 11th and 12th.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.560
Satellite images from August 15th

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.780
reveal traces of concentrated shelling

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.213
around Russian trenches
west of the village.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.780
The next day ISW's Frontline map

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.210
shows Russian forces
pushed Ukrainian troops

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.473
back across the river.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:31.440
(soldier shouting)
(gun firing)

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.780
But analysts say these
raids have already created

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.890
a headache for Moscow.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:38.250
(soldiers speaking in foreign language)

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.230
And the threat of more raids in the future

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.970
means Russia may need to choose

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.644
between risk and control of
part of its southern front

00:02:44.644 --> 00:02:46.890
(rocket launcher swooshing)

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.710
or defending other major hotspots.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.190
Russia has lost ground recently
in the Zaphorizhzhia region.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.560
Fighting continues around Bakhmut

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.830
and Russia is attempting an
offensive in the Northeast.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.560
By continuing to attack
along the Dnipro River,

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.530
Ukrainians are stretching
out Russian forces.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.470
And tying up troops here
means it's less likely

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.480
they can be sent to these other locations

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.454
where Russia needs them.

00:03:11.454 --> 00:03:13.080
(dramatic music)

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.440
Russia's US Embassy didn't
respond to requests for comment

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.930
and Ukrainian special
forces declined to comment

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.377
on the attacks in Kozachi Laheri.

00:03:21.377 --> 00:03:22.680
(engine rumbling)

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.744
In the months ahead,
defending the Southern front

00:03:24.744 --> 00:03:28.031
may become an even bigger
task for the Russians.

00:03:28.031 --> 00:03:30.448
(gun firing)

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.510
North of the now destroyed Kakhovka Dam,

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.313
the riverbed is drying up.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.820
Analysts say this could
allow the Ukrainian army

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.720
to send forces across on
foot or in military vehicles,

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.670
putting even further pressure on Russia's

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.628
already thinly stretched forces.

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:52.333
(dramatic music)

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:57.333
(soldiers shouting)
(guns firing)

